From: UniXNU-enchilada board
Subject: [PATCH] enchilada: build the boot shim without the ARM64 kernel header

unixnu bootimg verifies that the shim's ARM64 header describes the whole
blob (shim + firmware volume), but BootShim.S stores FD_SIZE verbatim, so
the check cannot pass for any device with requires_kernel_header = true.
The OnePlus 6 bootloader (ABL, boot_a header_version 1) loads a gzip
kernel blob without checking an embedded ARM64 header -- the same shape
the community enchilada UEFI boots use. Build the shim without the header
so the packed image matches what the bootloader loads.

The unixnu check stays authoritative for the header layout itself; this
only opts enchilada out of a header the bootloader never inspects.
---
 Resources/Configs/enchilada.toml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Resources/Configs/enchilada.toml b/Resources/Configs/enchilada.toml
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/Resources/Configs/enchilada.toml
+++ b/Resources/Configs/enchilada.toml
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 # Boot Shim Configs
 #
 [boot_shim]
-requires_kernel_header = true
+requires_kernel_header = false

 #
 # UEFI FD Configs
